ion contains a full description of the architectural decisions.&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;skos:definition&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;An Architectural Decision Record (ADR) is a document that captures the key decisions made during the architectural design and development of a software system. It is used to record the rationale, alternatives considered, and trade-offs made during the decision-making process, as well as the context and implications of each decision.&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:definitionSource&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;Architectural Decision Records&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:definitionSourceReference&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;https:\/\/adr.github.io\/&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:adr_context&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;The context explains why we need to make a decision. It also describes the alternatives along with the pros and cons.&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:adr_decision&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;The decision describes the justification for why the particular solution was accepted. It has more emphasis on the why rather than the how.&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:adr_status&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;[Proposed (under review)|Accepted (approved and ready for implementation)|Superseded (superseded by another decision)]&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:adr_consecuences&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;The consequences section contains information about the overall impact of an architectural decision. Every decision has trade-offs. That\u2019s why it\u2019s crucial to include the analysis to provide a clear picture.&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:iopDimension&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;Governance IoP&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:view&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;Interoperability Motivation View&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:concept&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock&quot;}]}</ns1:properties>
  </skos:Concept>

  <skos:Concept rdf:about="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/AchieveInteroperabilityGoal">
    <skos:inScheme rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8"/>
    <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Achieve Interoperability</skos:prefLabel>
    <skos:definition xml:lang="en">DEFINITION:
Achieve Interoperability ABB is a Goal. For the purpose of the EIF, interoperability is the ability of organisations to interact towards mutually beneficial goals, involving the sharing of information and knowledge between these organisations, through the business processes they support, by means of the exchange of data between their ICT systems.
The interoperability model which is applicable to all digital public services and may also be considered as an integral element of the interoperability-by-design paradigm. It includes: four layers of interoperability: legal, organisational, semantic and technical.

Source: EIF
(&lt;a href=&quot;https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/sites/isa/files/eif_brochure_final.pdf&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://ec.europa.eu/isa2/sites/isa/files/eif_brochure_final.pdf&lt;/a&gt;)</skos:definition>
    <skos:broaderTransitive rdf:resource="http://data.europa.eu/dr8/viewpoint/EnterpriseArchitectureFrameworkAlignmentGuidelinesViewpoint"/>
    <ns1:properties rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">{&quot;namespaces&quot;:{&quot;rdf&quot;:{&quot;namespace&quot;:&quot;rdf:&quot;,&quot;uri&quot;:&quot;http:\/\/www.w3.org\/1999\/02\/22-rdf-syntax-ns#&quot;},&quot;skos&quot;:{&quot;namespace&quot;:&quot;skos:&quot;,&quot;uri&quot;:&quot;http:\/\/www.w3.org\/2004\/02\/skos\/core#&quot;},&quot;dct&quot;:{&quot;namespace&quot;:&quot;dct:&quot;,&quot;uri&quot;:&quot;http:\/\/purl.org\/dc\/terms\/&quot;},&quot;eira&quot;:{&quot;namespace&quot;:&quot;eira:&quot;,&quot;uri&quot;:&quot;http:\/\/data.europa.eu\/dr8\/&quot;}},&quot;rows&quot;:[{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;rdf:type&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;http:\/\/www.w3.org\/2004\/02\/skos\/core#Concept&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;skos:notation&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;Properties of Achieve Interoperability&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;dct:identifier&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;http:\/\/data.europa.eu\/dr8\/AchieveInteroperabilityGoal_Properties&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;dct:identifier&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;http:\/\/data.europa.eu\/dr8\/AchieveInteroperabilityGoal&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;skos:prefLabel&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;Properties of Achieve Interoperability&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:PURI&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;http:\/\/data.europa.eu\/dr8\/AchieveInteroperabilityGoal&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;dct:type&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;eira:AchieveInteroperabilityGoal&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;dct:modified&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;2023-04-18&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;skos:definition&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;Achieve Interoperability ABB is a Goal. For the purpose of the EIF, interoperability is the ability of organisations to interact towards mutually beneficial goals, involving the sharing of information and knowledge between these organisations, through the business processes they support, by means of the exchange of data between their ICT systems.&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:definitionSource&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;EIF&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:definitionSourceReference&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;https:\/\/ec.europa.eu\/isa2\/sites\/isa\/files\/eif_brochure_final.pdf&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;skos:note&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;The interoperability model which is applicable to all digital public services and may also be considered as an integral element of the interoperability-by-design paradigm. It includes: four layers of interoperability: legal, organisational, semantic and technical.&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:concept&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;eira:ArchitectureBuildingBlock&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:iopDimension&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;Behavioral IoP&quot;},{&quot;property&quot;:&quot;eira:viewpoint&quot;,&quot;value&quot;:&quot;Enterprise Architecture Framework alignment guidelines viewpoint&quot;}]}</ns1:properties>
